            },
            {
                "entry_id": "f944ffab-7a65-3c91-93ea-82e4c47ec960",
                "word": "leveller",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3190039b-46e6-4f3d-a04c-9619f2a09447",
                        "entry_id": "f944ffab-7a65-3c91-93ea-82e4c47ec960",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "levellers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba3d85b6-c9ef-3218-a960-ce862450a7a4",
                        "entry_id": "f944ffab-7a65-3c91-93ea-82e4c47ec960",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person or thing that levels."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7af7ba17-0e93-4d02-ba98-b4e7f15a961f",
                                "sense_id": "ba3d85b6-c9ef-3218-a960-ce862450a7a4",
                                "text": "I adjusted the leveller built into each leg of the table, but it still wobbled."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35f2389a-14fb-4a12-bb64-fcd1b1ed6c8d",
                                "sense_id": "ba3d85b6-c9ef-3218-a960-ce862450a7a4",
                                "text": "A soil leveller is used to prepare the field before sowing."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "56c1b95b-564e-3b0a-b689-5751f0d56446",
                        "entry_id": "f944ffab-7a65-3c91-93ea-82e4c47ec960",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something that transcends people’s differences (such as social class, wealth, etc.); something that tends to eliminate advantages and disadvantages."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd8a34d4-579f-43fc-aec9-423a0206112d",
                                "sense_id": "56c1b95b-564e-3b0a-b689-5751f0d56446",
                                "text": "Conversation is not to be met with in large and mixed companies; and a card-table, considered as an universal leveller, may have its use, by placing the weak and timid on a par with the most lively and overbearing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec3747b4-9b39-4f12-88fd-05dbbe903a6f",
                                "sense_id": "56c1b95b-564e-3b0a-b689-5751f0d56446",
                                "text": "All the captives, the innocent as well as the guilty, gladly subscribed to the terms; for they found themselves in a temporary duresse which did not admit of any fair argument of the merits of the case, and there is no leveller so effectual as a common misfortune."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3a30bf0-9f78-4ee0-b28c-fca473ecb81c",
                                "sense_id": "56c1b95b-564e-3b0a-b689-5751f0d56446",
                                "text": "Everything about the old man was clean, if coarse; and, with Death, the leveller, so close at hand, it was the labourer who made the first advances, and put out his horny hand to the Squire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3611d408-dce5-4608-8cfb-8d7498915c6c",
                                "sense_id": "56c1b95b-564e-3b0a-b689-5751f0d56446",
                                "text": "The army is viewed not only as a social leveler but also as a means of unifying a country with three cultures and four languages."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3c8e54ea-1422-3f75-abe3-985cc7e1e5d8",
                        "entry_id": "f944ffab-7a65-3c91-93ea-82e4c47ec960",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person holding a political opinion in favor of eliminating disparities between the haves and the have-nots."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a357ab83-f4bc-41e2-8b67-67050037ac22",
                                "sense_id": "3c8e54ea-1422-3f75-abe3-985cc7e1e5d8",
                                "text": "Among the independents, who, in general, were for having no eccleſiaſtical ſubordination, a ſet of men grew up called Levellers, who diſallowed all ſubordination whatſoever, and declared that they would have no other chaplain, king, or general, but Chriſt. They declared that all men were equal; that all degrees and ranks should be levelled, and an exact partition of property eſtabliſhed in the nation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c724a157-d26f-4f4f-8994-2d6e33060003",
                                "sense_id": "3c8e54ea-1422-3f75-abe3-985cc7e1e5d8",
                                "text": "[…] there was no sympathy and connection between the upper and the lower people of the Irish. To one who had been bred so much abroad as myself, this difference between Catholic and Protestant was doubly striking; and though as firm as a rock in my own faith, yet I could not help remembering my grandfather held a different one, and wondering that there should be such a political difference between the two. I passed among my neighbours for a dangerous leveller, for entertaining and expressing such opinions […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bcbe10ad-618d-3a09-8d24-ea9d6837025e",
                        "entry_id": "f944ffab-7a65-3c91-93ea-82e4c47ec960",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An equaliser."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b51d83f5-a076-46b3-8aa2-7cdb21b9046a",
                                "sense_id": "bcbe10ad-618d-3a09-8d24-ea9d6837025e",
                                "text": "Cardiff pressed for a leveller to force the tie into penalties, but Stoke comfortably held out and Walters added his second finishing from a tight angle after his first shot was beaten back to him by Heaton."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "08bcdf06-1595-4d0f-b980-77670d237024",
                        "source_entry_id": "f944ffab-7a65-3c91-93ea-82e4c47ec960",
                        "source_sense_description": "person or thing",
                        "target_lang_word": "уравни́тель",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "уравни́тель",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2766a566-799e-33b9-a5b7-51cec0c13417",
                                        "entry_id": "ea0562fc-200c-3749-849c-d34aceae38a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "тот, кто уравнивает кого-либо, что-либо; сторонник (социального) равенства"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14816eec-8042-4dc6-8a96-a5cedd31412e",
                                                "sense_id": "2766a566-799e-33b9-a5b7-51cec0c13417",
                                                "text": "Вы истинный член вашей фамилии: все Романовы революционеры и уравнители, ― скажет Пушкин в 1834 году младшему брату Александра, Михаилу Павловичу."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f85ff4ff-0e71-349e-9dfc-df45282dace7",
                                        "entry_id": "ea0562fc-200c-3749-849c-d34aceae38a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "истор. в период гражданской войны в Англии (1642–1649) — представитель партии радикалов, выступавших за упразднение монархии и широкие реформы"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f05c051-6563-454d-bd38-8158fb797647",
                                                "sense_id": "f85ff4ff-0e71-349e-9dfc-df45282dace7",
                                                "text": "В таком смысле высказывались предшественники современного радикализма в Англии, так называемые «левеллеры», или уравнители, и то же на все лады повторяли одинаково и Камил Демулен, и Кондорсе, другими словами, столько же якобинцы, сколько и жирондисты."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "уравни́тель",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9a3b311-ecb8-32ef-8922-aa3f2138bdd3",
                                        "entry_id": "44f1d1d9-4ad5-32b0-a449-cc3665edf46a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "техн. машина, механизм, служащие для уравнения, выравнивания чего-либо"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2a9a1e0-41fb-4f57-a0e2-27e19a469ab0",
                                                "sense_id": "c9a3b311-ecb8-32ef-8922-aa3f2138bdd3",
                                                "text": "В настоящее время известно несколько центробежных уравнителей, которых скорость вращения остается одна и та же при всех возможных положениях подвижной муфты."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53f22306-c364-4b21-b8b8-62cc678badb4",
                                                "sense_id": "c9a3b311-ecb8-32ef-8922-aa3f2138bdd3",
                                                "text": "Она имеет только время, измеряемое звонками топочного уравнителя и числом подбрасываемых лопат."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cde75b04-7272-35f7-b8cc-4312c0d288da",
                                        "entry_id": "44f1d1d9-4ad5-32b0-a449-cc3665edf46a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "матем. множество аргументов, в которых две или более функции имеют равные значения"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c7869c7-88ee-4621-bcf1-158a2bec3d06",
                                                "sense_id": "cde75b04-7272-35f7-b8cc-4312c0d288da",
                                                "text": "Двоичный уравнитель (то есть уравнитель только двух функций) также называется ядром разности."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd9f01bf-3653-32ab-b7b7-583987124b1b",
                                        "entry_id": "44f1d1d9-4ad5-32b0-a449-cc3665edf46a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "то, что уравнивает кого-либо, что-либо"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0daac744-2f6b-4673-872a-4dea5b4489c4",
                                                "sense_id": "cd9f01bf-3653-32ab-b7b7-583987124b1b",
                                                "text": "Видимо, именно в это время американский литератор Рэньон выдал свой афоризм «Револьвер ― уравнитель шансов»."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
